The Day 241 plan is written: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The plan commit didn't happen, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore and git add refused it. The planned command ends in || true, so this looks like the harness's normal case rather than a failure, but nothing from this phase is in git.

Task 1 (product, capability gap): when the model's bash call times out, return the output it printed so far instead of only "timed out". Right now that output is thrown away, so the model re-runs a hung build or test blind and pays a second full timeout. yoyo's own dependency (yoagent 0.25.15) and Claude Code's 2026-10-26 release both already do this, so the wording comes from yoagent. The result stays an error. A command that printed nothing keeps exactly today's message. src/tools.rs is already over its size-register entry (5258 against 5247), so all the tests go in a new sibling file. Positive control: break the fix, watch the test fail, then restore it.

Task 2 (product, Fixes #1087): yoyo grep hello a on a matching single file outside a git repo says "No matches found." and exits 1. The fix is grep's -H flag in the plain, count and context branches. Tests also go in a sibling file, since src/commands_search.rs is also over its register entry (4582 against 4573). Directory paths, . and the git-repo case must stay byte-identical. Searching two paths at once (yoyo grep hello a b) is a separate bug, so it gets filed as its own issue before the push, so that "Fixes #1087" doesn't close the only place it's tracked.

Why slot 2 isn't the oldest backlog item: I went through the oldest ones first:
• #1012 (price drift): close as not-planned. Every remaining drift row now needs a typed --model to hit, and the two places that read low have moved to #1084.
• #1014 (spawn write tap): keep open with a comment. Wiring the tap into background workers isn't just plumbing. A background worker runs while the main checkout keeps being edited, so a before/after diff would blame the worker for the parent's edits. That needs a decision before any code.
• #1018 (durable todos): still has open design questions, so it isn't ready for a slice.

